// The annotation form is the base form the block is grouping sugar for — "full equivalence", as
// the parser puts it. So for a code tier, `@debug fn f()` IS `@debug { fn f() {} }`: whatever the
// block admits, the annotation admits, and both strip on a normal run.
//
// This is a regression guard. While unifying the attachment model I read `debug`'s empty site set
// as "attaches to nothing" and made `@debug fn f()` an error. The empty set was not a decision to
// forbid the annotation — nobody had considered the annotation form for `debug` at all — and
// rejecting it removed expressiveness (a debug-only helper) for no gain.
// expect: stdout "ok"
// expect: exit 0
@debug
fn debug_only_helper(): int { return 41 }

@debug {
  fn also_debug_only(): int { return 42 }
}

echo "ok"
